{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"At Sāketa: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja68'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 68 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>8. Sāketajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>At Sāketa: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yasmiṁ mano nivisati, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>In whom the mind settles, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>cittañcāpi pasīdati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and the heart too is confident—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Adiṭṭhapubbake pose, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>gladly one would trust in </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kāmaṁ tasmimpi vissase”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that man not seen before. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Sāketajātakaṁ aṭṭhamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
